<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian July housing materials prices flat.</title>
<headline>Australian July housing materials prices flat.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian house building materials prices were unchanged in July from the previous month, but stood 0.8 percent lower than a year before, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Other building materials prices fell 0.1 percent in the month, creating a 0.2 percent annual rise.  </p>
<p>The annual rate of housing materials inflation has varied between minus 0.6 percent and minus 1.0 since February.</p>
<p>For other materials the annual rate has been falling consistendly since a year ago, when it was 2.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
